WEBVTT

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:28.650
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:28.650
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:28.650
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:54.230 --> 00:02:02.650
The Duelist
Chapter I

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.730
In January of Imperial Year 483...

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.850
...having been promoted to Lieutenant because of his actions aboard the Hameln II...

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:19.850
...Reinhard, along with Kircheis,
who remained an Ensign...

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:24.870
...was assigned to desk work at the Inspection Department of the Ministry of the Military upon his return to Odin.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.120
How disappointing.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.100
That I was transferred to office
duty in the Ministry of the Military...

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:39.830
...to be buried under
such boring documents.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:44.780
At least, if I had continued my
tour of duty on the destroyer...

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:49.430
...I might have had opportunities to make a name for myself on the battlefield.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.740
Doesn't this bore you, Kircheis ?

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.570
I'm bored, too.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:08.550
If you continue to only fight piles
of documents in a place like this...

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:11.100
...you lose sight of the
true nature of war.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.000
The casualty numbers become
just another statistic...

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.850
...and makes you forget that
each soldier has a life of his own.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.690
You're right.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:24.500
Having been to the front lines,
I know what you mean.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:31.380
Most aristocrats hate to go to the front lines and prefer to stay behind for desk work.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:34.600
That's how they become
oblivious to other people's pain.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.940
Being here makes me
realize that profoundly.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:42.100
Lord Reinhard, you won't
ever forget that, will you ?

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:47.960
When I get to lead a large fleet,
I'll always want to be on the front line.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:53.240
I'll command from the front lines, and
lead all my troops into battle personally.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:55.560
That's the kind of
commander I want to be.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.590
What's this ?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:00.890
What's wrong ?

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.260
Take a look at the numbers here.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:09.850
These are the figures for the supplies and resources sent from Iserlohn Fortress to each front line base.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.500
But there are large discrepancies between the
amount shipped and the amount consumed.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:19.800
These look too large to
be occasional clerical errors.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.640
Lord Reinhard is good.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:25.390
Even when he seems uninterested, he's
paying close attention to the things he has to.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:29.050
Kircheis, I need more evidence.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.570
Gather some more data.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.510
Yes, sir.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.650
Good investigative work.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:54.470
I'd like to say that,
but this is meaningless.

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:02.200
Respectfully, sir, it doesn't
seem "meaningless" to us.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.280
I agree.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:11.080
This indicates the possible misappropriation of resources shipped to the front line.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.950
I think it advisable to report
this up the chain of command...

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:17.220
...and request that an inspector
be dispatched immediately.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:21.150
You're still green, so you 
may not be aware of it...

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:25.650
...but things like this happen all the time. It's an open secret.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:30.360
It's called a "necessary evil."

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:35.390
If there were no such perks, no one would want to be assigned to the front lines.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:38.900
But if that's true, what's the Inspection Department supposed to do ?

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:43.020
To put limits on the "necessary evil."

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:45.910
There has to be some degree of moderation, even for private appropriation.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:49.050
We're here to prevent the 
complete loss of that "moderation."

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:55.500
But what kind of official
explanation can be given...

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.360
...to these discrepancies
in the delivered quantities ?

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:02.790
It'll be explained as "loss 
of resources during shipment."

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:10.400
For example, food can go stale at the shipment port while its destination remains undecided.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.000
And that often happens in reality, too.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:17.850
Actually, about 1/3 of what you pointed out is probably the amount of food that went stale.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:23.850
Besides, we can recover the loss by
just collecting it again from the people.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:26.500
It's not something 
to be upset about.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:29.450
No one has anything to gain if we make a big deal of this.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:33.200
You should just learn 
the way of the world.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:46.510
What indolence, negligence, retrogression - how thoroughly corrupt !

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.150
I agree.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:52.840
If you're removed from the front lines, is this how degenerate you get ?

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:58.810
No, the actual crimes are taking place on the front line, so the front line is also corrupt in its own way.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:04.310
Kircheis, the military of this nation is totally
rotten, from its core to the ends of its limbs.

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:07.100
You're right, Lord Reinhard...

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:08.530
...but you're talking too loud.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.100
Lord Reinhard, it's precisely
because the military is corrupt...

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:22.300
...because this nation is corrupt, that what you intend to do is meaningful.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:26.500
Please keep to the moral high ground for now,
but right now you should maintain a low profile.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:32.120
When you gain higher rank, you can end all of this iniquity and degeneration.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.490
Until then, please be patient.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:44.240
I know, but being unable to reason with them, even on a petty issue like this...

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.510
I'm completely powerless
within this large organization.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:50.520
Lord Reinhard...

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.610
Oh, Kircheis.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:00.750
I want more power.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.890
I can't do anything
as a simple lieutenant.

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:07.630
I can't do anything for my sister, either.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:08.770
I want power.

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:10.640
I want to rise in
the world more quickly.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.200
Please don't be hasty.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:15.100
You're already a lieutenant half a year
after graduating from military prep school.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:18.000
You're climbing the promotional
ladder more quickly...

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.750
...than any child from an esteemed
lineage of the aristocrats ever could.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:28.610
Even so, I'm so tired of doing petty jobs in a corrupt place like this.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:31.960
Don't you smell the
putrid odor, Kircheis ?

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.870
I feel like I'm suffocating.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:38.180
I've grown to hate breathing the totally rotten air of Odin !

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:41.910
Would you like to file
another transfer request ?

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.050
The front lines.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.740
I want to go to the front lines.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:53.530
The front lines have their own kind of corruption, but it's still better than a stagnant place like this.

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:59.000
But if you stay on Odin, you'll have
opportunities to see Lady Annerose.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.300
Yeah, you're right...

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.040
...but no, I can't.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:10.210
I want to save my sister 
from this foul-smelling place.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:13.050
Besides, each time I want
to meet with my sister...

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:18.540
...I have to ask the Kaiser's 
permission, and that's intolerable !

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.890
Lord Reinhard...

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:29.400
Permission to visit Annerose's house, a resident of the Emperor's palace...

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:32.610
...is not easily granted, even to Reinhard, her blood relative.

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:42.980
A few days later, the two finally had an opportunity to meet with Annerose...

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:48.300
...but it was an arranged "chance" meeting at the residence of Viscountess Schafhausen...

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:50.260
...Annerose's friend at the Court.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:59.090
Moreover, they said it was for my own good that
I do nothing about it and further, for yours as well.

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:05.950
How spineless.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:08.540
The Ministry of the Military is, after all, a government office.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.800
So, is that the end of it ?

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:13.550
As a formality, they
accepted the report, but...

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:18.360
Well, they'll say they'll do
something about it, but they won't.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:23.470
At least no one will do anything on his own responsibility.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:24.800
That's their style.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:31.030
If they take action and somehow interfere
with the interest of the brass or aristocrats...

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:33.690
...they believe that their
promotion could be in jeopardy.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.400
How useless these men are.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:43.140
Oh, you two are fine.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:47.670
You still have the potential to grow into men of dignity in the future.

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:50.460
But you shouldn't 
become petty adults, okay ?

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:57.500
Lord Reinhard might be dissatisfied with being treated like a child...

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:01.500
...but well, we can't
measure up to this baroness.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:04.930
Of course we can depend on her as Lady Annerose's ally.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:14.120
But you two, this is not a reasonable world, 
so if you work too hard, you might make enemies.

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:15.230
So be careful.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.270
Is something wrong, Viscountess ?

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.690
You seem rather sad today.

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:50.280
No, it's nothing...

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.150
It's because of "that affair," isn't it ?

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:56.200
"That affair" ?

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:57.150
To tell you the truth...

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.320
Baroness...

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.480
It's okay, we can tell them.

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:04.060
But...

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:06.430
Don't worry.

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:10.020
Annerose, do you know 
who Count Helksheimer is ?

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:12.690
Yes, but just the name.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:17.430
I think he's part of the clan of the Marquis of Littenheim, isn't he ?

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:20.090
You haven't heard of his reputation ?

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.340
No...

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:23.000
Has this Count done something ?

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:25.500
It's such an outrage.

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:32.090
In a mine belonging to Viscount 
Schafhausen's family enterprises...

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:35.500
...a natural hydro-metal
vein was discovered.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:43.910
But the Helksheimers are trying to lay claim to the mine and selfishly putting up a dispute.

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:50.410
To begin with, Helksheimer is a slimeball who thinks he has bragging rights...

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:52.550
...because he's part of an esteemed lineage aristocratic clan.

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:55.050
He's greedy, snaky, and lewd.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:02.440
But anyway, it's an important fact that he's such a lecher.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:08.280
When he approaches a lady, he's forceful, abusive, and shameless in his manners.

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:13.020
Oh, you two are too young
to hear about things like that.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:24.050
Aside from that, the issue of mining
rights can be resolved in court, can't it ?

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:27.400
That's why he's a slimeball.

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:31.750
He knows he has no chance
in a legitimate civil trial...

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:35.380
...he made a challenge, forcing
resolution of the dispute by duel.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:38.610
Duel ?

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:44.970
It's not just the Count; it's a favorite
practice of aristocrats to pick a quarrel...

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:49.540
...propose a duel, and carry through with their unreasonable demands.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:53.300
Of course, those aristocrats
never fight themselves.

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:58.720
There are professional duelists who undertake such duels, and they fight as their agents{of the aristocrats}.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:02.970
Then there is no need for the 
Viscount himself to fight, is there ?

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:08.800
The problem is that there is no duelist who will fight on behalf of the Viscount's family.

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:09.700
Isn't that right ?

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.640
How could that happen ?

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:21.050
Helksheimer and his patron, the Marquis of Littenheim, took measures to make sure...

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:24.940
...that no one would become the agent for Viscount Schafhausen.

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:26.660
How despicable !

00:14:27.690 --> 00:14:30.180
So they made sure they'd win.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:35.550
So what are you planning to do ?

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:42.210
Well, since we can't find an agent,
either my husband himself has to fight...

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:45.500
...or we'll have to forfeit the duel and accept their demands.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:49.100
But as you know, my
husband is a quiet person...

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:54.240
...whose only hobbies are studying
herbal plants and reading travelogues.

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:57.050
He's not good at fighting at all.

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:59.330
Then are you going to 
meet their demands ?

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.230
Reinhard...

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:11.490
I'm sorry...

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:17.640
I'm sorry too, to bother you
with such a private affair...

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:22.050
...and take away your precious
time with one another.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:28.640
Well, I'm sure you two have much to talk about, so we should retire, shouldn't we ?

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:31.270
Please wait, Viscountess.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.480
Huh ?

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:39.710
The agent for the duel, can that role be assumed by anyone ?

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:42.850
Yes...

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:49.480
Then, I will undertake it.

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:52.950
How wonderful !

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:54.580
Reinhard !

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:55.820
Lord Reinhard.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.850
Oh no, I can't accept your offer...

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:06.550
No, I can't just sit silently when my sister's friend is in trouble.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:09.730
And you've always
been a big help to us.

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:12.970
This time around,
I'd like to be of use to you.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.100
But that's...

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.100
Please don't worry.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:19.060
I may not look like much,
but I'm a military officer.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.590
I'm used to handling weapons.

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:26.080
The opposition's duelist may be a professional, but I am also a professional at fighting.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:29.310
I will not be out-dueled.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:33.750
Or does the Viscountess
have doubts about my skills ?

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:37.030
No, that's not the issue...

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:45.030
Lady Annerose must be
having mixed feelings.

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:48.000
Of course, she feels more
strongly than anything...

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.060
...that she doesn't want Lord Reinhard to do anything dangerous.

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:55.970
But in a Court where 
she has many enemies...

00:16:55.970 --> 00:17:02.750
...Viscountess Schafhausen is, along with
Baroness Westpfahle, one of her only true friends.

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:08.000
She herself must be feeling she 
would like to help the Viscountess...

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.440
...so it must be difficult for her to tell Lord Reinhard to reconsider.

00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:16.350
Lord Reinhard, I will take on the task.

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:26.120
I hate to say it, Kircheis, but the one who made the offer first gets the job.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:28.350
I don't plan on conceding to you the honor of being the agent.

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:35.230
But, Lord Reinhard, you don't have to put yourself in danger; I'll do it.

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:40.560
Kircheis, you impudently think you're the more skilled fighter, don't you ?

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:42.120
No.

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.150
Not by any means.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:46.760
Then just leave it to me this time.

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:50.300
But what if anything should happen ?

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:53.630
Oh, Sieg, you shouldn't worry about that.

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:59.450
The duel is more of a ritual than anything else, and it hardly ever poses a risk to life.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:03.100
The only person who is allowed to call me Sieg is Lady Annerose, but...

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:08.850
Making your opponent surrender while injuring him as little as possible is considered a "good" duel.

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:13.500
In the unlikely event where a duelist kills his opponent, that is considered a "low" manner of winning...

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:16.640
...and the duelist will be the
laughingstock of aristocratic society.

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:19.690
You shouldn't kill 
your opponent either.

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:22.520
In the unlikely event that happens...

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:26.940
...you can't be held criminally accountable for what happens in a duel but your reputation would suffer.

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:30.050
You can count on me.

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:31.610
Lord Reinhard.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:33.480
Don't be a nag, Kircheis.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.120
Once in a while, you
can leave things to me.

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.850
"Once in a while" ?

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:39.800
You always have all the fun...

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:43.000
So does this suit you, Viscountess ?

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:45.600
Um, but no...

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.050
It's okay, take his offer.

00:18:48.050 --> 00:18:50.100
B...but...

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:56.400
Everything will be fine.

00:18:56.400 --> 00:19:00.000
I'll make the arrangements.
There's nothing to worry about.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.700
Okay, Annerose ?

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:04.750
Now that the matter's decided,
I have to work on the preparations.

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:07.040
We need a costume, too.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.410
So just count on me.

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:23.850
In the end, Annerose did
not actively dissuade him...

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:28.280
...so things were settled as Reinhard accepted to become the agent.

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:37.400
I wonder if my sister is upset...?

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:45.140
What do you think ?

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:48.970
She seemed to be 
more worried than upset.

00:19:49.970 --> 00:19:52.150
Such a thorny attitude...

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:54.090
...you're the one who's angry ?

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:59.950
Don't mind me, but please don't make Lady Annerose worry so much.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:03.210
Don't say that.

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:08.000
It's not like I accepted this because I was bored with my desk job and wanted to vent my anger.

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:15.280
Right now, I can't do 
anything for my sister.

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:20.760
Something like this, something as indirect as this, I wanted to at least do something.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:22.060
For my sister.

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:25.840
Lord Reinhard.

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:29.710
Lord Reinhard is suffering, too.

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:32.940
I understand.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:35.750
So that nothing injurious 
happens to you, Lord Reinhard...

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:37.850
...I will assist you
as best as I can.

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:45.520
As much as I can, in order to 
save Lady Annerose from worry.

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:49.720
I'll count on you.

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:53.380
Then first, do some research
on the conventions of dueling.

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:56.550
Lord Reinhard, how much
do you know about it ?

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:58.320
I don't know much in detail.

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:02.690
As I recall, there may be
some tedious rules.

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:06.080
You accepted a duel on the basis of such hazy knowledge as that ?

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:08.170
Yeah...

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:12.950
Don't be so shocked.

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:16.870
In essence, I just need to choose a gun
or sword and defeat my opponent, right ?

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:18.890
That's easy.

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:24.850
But I think there may be some 
manners or rules, so those details...{I want you to research}

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:31.090
Oh well, we might be having a long, tough journey ahead.

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:39.320
Kircheis was troubled, but actually, there was no substantial danger at this point.

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:46.050
Just as Baroness Westpfahle said...

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:52.350
...duels were more like games, and were no longer a matter of life-or-death.

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:58.300
It has become more like gambling,
especially among the high aristocrats...

00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:02.610
...who put their pride and interests on the line in these fights between their agents.

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:15.050
Many aristocrats other than the involved parties join in as spectators and in fact, bets are often made.

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:18.650
In other words,
it's more like a show...

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:24.050
...and since the duelists are professionals, they rarely let their opponents die.

00:22:25.050 --> 00:22:29.500
In that regard, there was
no danger to Reinhard's life.

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:34.140
Up to this point, at least.

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:52.430
What ?

00:22:52.430 --> 00:22:53.850
That brat will be...?

